y we raise the flag  every day we say the pledge of  allegiance  i think it's sad that it's not every day  we honor wonderful people like you  yes we have memorials but we don't  always say thank you in words like a  letter or card like this  thank you i hope after everything you've  done for our country you will live a  long and happy life i am unbelievably  proud of your service  you are one of many soldiers that helped  lead our country to freedom  you will be honored and known for your  great and unselfish sacrifice  our country would not be the same  without you veterans all of the veterans  out there are all heroes  i hope you enjoy your flight to  washington dc the memorial is really  beautiful i hope you like it as much as  i do  sincerely benjamin yeah hannah flynn  paul  maddy many thank yous  memory  thank you very much ella and very thanks  to you sweetheart this is a great letter  and  makes me feel really good i want to tell  benjamin he's going to have a good life  if you see a veteran on the street just  say hello  it's a wonderful experience for any of  us  and it's very memorable i'm not used to  getting getting that kind of accolades  it's like a somebody in your dreams  thank you so much  yeah  thank you  you know it's so wonderful is that they  don't seek the accolades they don't seek  the praise you can see how touched they  are but it's never ever ever too late to  say thank you and to let you know that  you're appreciated in whatever it is  that you do never yeah for every team  that i played on i told my coaches  whether it was practice game day at an  event yeah if i saw a man or woman that  serves this country or has served this  country i was going to stop everything i  was doing to send a message to the young  players that we need to show gratitude  to them so i would encourage anybody  just like you heard if you see someone  that serves this country or have served  just walk over to him and say thank you  that's it just that little bit 